## VPC Endpoints

### 1. Gateway Endpoints

**Services:** S3, DynamoDB

```bash
# Create S3 Gateway Endpoint
aws ec2 create-vpc-endpoint \
  --vpc-id vpc-12345678 \
  --service-name com.amazonaws.us-east-1.s3 \
  --route-table-ids rtb-12345678 \
  --vpc-endpoint-type Gateway

# Output: vpc-endpoint-id vpc-ep-12345678

# Example use cases:
# - Private EC2 → S3 (no internet needed)
# - Download large files without NAT Gateway cost
# - Enhanced security (traffic stays within AWS)

# Create DynamoDB Gateway Endpoint
aws ec2 create-vpc-endpoint \
  --vpc-id vpc-12345678 \
  --service-name com.amazonaws.us-east-1.dynamodb \
  --route-table-ids rtb-private-1a rtb-private-1b

# Verify endpoint
aws ec2 describe-vpc-endpoints \
  --vpc-endpoint-ids vpc-ep-12345678

# Update route table for endpoint
aws ec2 modify-vpc-endpoint \
  --vpc-endpoint-id vpc-ep-12345678 \
  --route-table-ids rtb-12345678 rtb-67890123
```

### 2. Interface Endpoints

**Services:** SNS, SQS, Kinesis, EC2, Lambda, CloudWatch, Secrets Manager, etc.

```bash
# Create Interface Endpoint (SNS example)
aws ec2 create-vpc-endpoint \
  --vpc-id vpc-12345678 \
  --vpc-endpoint-type Interface \
  --service-name com.amazonaws.us-east-1.sns \
  --subnet-ids subnet-private-1a subnet-private-1b \
  --security-group-ids sg-12345678

# Output:
# vpc-endpoint-id: vpc-ep-12345678
# Network interfaces created automatically
# Private IP assigned (10.0.x.x)
# DNS name provided

# List available services
aws ec2 describe-vpc-endpoint-services \
  --query 'ServiceNames' | head -20

# Verify interface endpoint
aws ec2 describe-vpc-endpoints \
  --vpc-endpoint-ids vpc-ep-12345678

# Use endpoint in application
# Default SNS endpoint: https://sns.us-east-1.amazonaws.com
# VPC Endpoint: https://vpce-12345678.sns.us-east-1.vpce.amazonaws.com
# Or use: https://sns.us-east-1.amazonaws.com (AWS uses endpoint automatically)
```

### 3. Endpoint Policy

```bash
# Create S3 endpoint with policy (restrict to specific bucket)
cat > s3-endpoint-policy.json << 'EOF'
{
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": [
        "s3:GetObject",
        "s3:PutObject"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::production-bucket/*"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
EOF

aws ec2 create-vpc-endpoint \
  --vpc-id vpc-12345678 \
  --service-name com.amazonaws.us-east-1.s3 \
  --route-table-ids rtb-12345678 \
  --policy-document file://s3-endpoint-policy.json

# Benefits of endpoint policy:
# - Restrict which AWS services can access
# - Control which buckets/resources
# - Security through principle of least privilege
```

### 4. Gateway vs Interface Endpoints

| Aspect | Gateway Endpoint | Interface Endpoint |
|--------|-----------------|-------------------|
| Services | S3, DynamoDB | Most AWS services |
| Type | Automatic routing | Requires DNS/IP |
| Cost | Free | $7.20/month + data |
| Where deployed | Route table entry | ENI in subnet |
| DNS | Automatic | Custom DNS entry |
| Security Group | N/A | Yes (required) |
| Availability | Automatic HA | Multi-AZ capable |

